WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.400
AI-Agent Search Engine that I built to research a question across
Google, Bing, and Reddit,

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.840
then synthesize the results into one clear answer.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:18.800
In the workflow diagram on the left, the user starts by entering a
question into the console.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:23.980
My LangGraph workflow then launches separate Google, Bing, and Reddit
search.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:29.340
The Reddit branches go deeper by using structured LLM output to select
useful posts, retrieve

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:34.220
comments, and feed that data into a dedicated analysis loop.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:40.500
After that, each source goes through its own analysis nodes, and the
final synthesis node

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.780
combines the finding into one response.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:48.700
In the console demo, you can see the system moving through each stage,
launching searches,

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:54.980
selecting Reddit URLs, retrieving comments, analyzing sources, and
printing the final answer.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.860
My role was designing and implementing the orchestration layer using
Python, LangGraph,

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:03.520
LangChain, OpenAI, Bright Data, and Pydantic.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:08.480
I'm especially proud of using structured output because it made the
agent more reliable and

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:09.680
easier to debug.
